      "text": "You can use multiplication to solve this problem. Multiply the number of lawns mowed by the amount Tyler earns per lawn. Then subtract the amount Tyler had to pay for gas.",
      "example": "Example: Gerald earned $25 a day washing cars. He washed cars for 5 days last month. He also had to pay $15 for cleaning supplies. How much money did Gerald make last month after expenses?",
      "result": "Money Made: $25 5 – $15 = $110",
